  "instance_name": "semiotic_projection_1",
  "label": "User projected onto the scene as the recipient of scolding advice",
  "description": "The user is projected onto the scene (scolding_meme) as the person being scolded for improper meme formatting. This projection is established through the textual material ('if you're gonna screenshot a meme') which directly addresses the viewer ('you'), and the visual material (Patrick_Stewart pointing sternly) which visually embodies the role of the scolding authority figure. The mapping is analogical: the viewer ('you') is projected onto Patrick_Stewart as the recipient of the scolding instruction.",
